    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d598">

                <pb facs="0761" n="749" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg749"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/1291: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-02-27T18:00:00-04:00">February 27,
                            1943—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1282. “For Harriman from Stettinius. Reference your 1391,<anchor n="65"
                        xml:id="d598-f1"/> full U.S. commitment for duraluminum has already been
                    met. Nevertheless, more duraluminum sheets have been and will continue to be
                    supplied to meet Soviet requests and in pro rata satisfaction of aluminum ingot
                    commitment. The increase we referred to is 1,300 tons aluminum ingots and 2,200
                    tons duraluminum sheets over and above total U.S. commitment for both
                    duraluminum and aluminum.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
